WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.890
Critics and audiences agree that Aquaman feels
like a breath of fresh air after drowning

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.400
in DC's murkier efforts.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.980
It's a light, funny adventure film anchored
by two charming leads and buoyed by eye-popping

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.620
visuals.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:16.240
But a vessel this large can only turn its
rudder so fast, and it's bound to have a few

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.160
barnacles still clinging to its hull.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:23.140
Prepare for spoilers, and continue full speed
ahead to the three best and three worst things

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.160
about Aquaman.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.020
Batman and Superman have some pretty iconic
bad guys always giving them grief.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.620
By contrast, Aquaman...doesn't.

00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:35.980
The movie introduces perhaps the two most
significant villains from the pages of Aquaman

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.140
comics, Black Manta and Ocean Master.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.800
Both of them are okay, but the story suffers
slightly from having two separate antagonists

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.610
diluting the story's central conflict.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.520
It's a problem all too common to superhero
movies.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.500
At least we know we'll get more of Black Manta
and that big laser-shooting helmet of his

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.680
in the inevitable sequel...

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.179
Jason Momoa was a highlight of Justice League,
and fans have been looking forward to more

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:00.030
of his likeable dirtbag embodiment of Arthur
Curry.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.060
Not only does the Aquaman solo movie live
up to its potential as a Momoa vehicle, it

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.560
supports him with one of the best casts yet
assembled for the DCEU.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.500
It's an eclectic ensemble with some surprising
cameos, but each gets a moment to shine and,

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.700
unlike some of the more convoluted comic movies
in recent memory, everyone's clearly on the

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.390
same page about what kind of strange adventure
they're on.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.970
Momoa continues his schtick as the buff, waterlogged
barfly with a heart of gold, but being the

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.860
center of attention allows him to add new
layers to the character.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.820
He lets Arthur's self-doubt bubble to the
surface in his most vulnerable moments, making

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.340
him endearing without sacrificing any of his
rowdy charm.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.790
Meanwhile, Amber Heard successfully leads
alongside him as Mera with a perfect balance

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.020
of fearsome focus and wide-eyed wonder.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.580
From her scene wandering Sicily with Arthur
to her battle through the city, Heard makes

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.220
Mera a true standout.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.100
Justice League formally introduced audiences
to Aquaman, but only had time for a brief

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.100
exploration of his Atlantean origins.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:58.280
Mera appeared in one sequence, in which Arthur
attempted to protect a Mother Box from Steppenwolf.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.640
Arthur expressed bitterness over being "abandoned"
by his mother, Queen Atlanna, and held her

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.660
neglect against the people of Atlantis.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.780
The Arthur we catch up with in Aquaman is
less angry at his mother — he's aware that

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.670
she was forced to return to the sea — and
learns that she was sacrificed to a monster-filled

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.700
place called the Trench for the crime of having
a half-breed son, filling him with grief and

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.200
guilt.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.800
The movie more or less has to undo the motivations
established in Justice League in order to

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.239
get his character arc moving in the right
direction.

00:02:24.239 --> 00:02:28.190
There's also a change in how Atlanteans communicate
— it seemed in Justice League that Arthur

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:32.629
and Mera could only talk inside an air bubble,
but Aquaman has its characters speak freely

00:02:32.629 --> 00:02:33.760
even when submerged.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.920
It makes sense that a movie set mostly underwater
would choose not to complicate its characters'

00:02:37.921 --> 00:02:42.150
ability to talk to each other in this way,
but it raises the question of why Justice

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.740
League introduced such a clunky conceit in
the first place.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:50.180
Fans might be slightly annoyed at Aquaman's
contradictions of established DCEU lore, but

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.420
this actually becomes one of its strongest
assets: the movie is completely unburdened

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.360
by connections to other movies, either past
or present.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.960
Where Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice nearly
drowned in set-ups and introductions designed

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:07.160
to pay off in future installments, Aquaman
floats free, unencumbered by the sort of franchise-minded

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.500
filmmaking that has sunk other comic book
movies.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.290
Aside from briefly mentioning Arthur's battle
with Steppenwolf, Aquaman contains no references

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.320
to any other DC characters not involved in
its hero's journey.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.700
No secret Lexcorp files, no foreshadowing
of cataclysmic events to come.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.790
It's just a straight-ahead adventure story
about Aquaman and his friends and enemies.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.310
It is, in fact, a perfect jumping-on point
for newcomers to the DC Universe — something

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.570
Warner Bros. sorely needs after the convoluted
webs of its predecessors proved off-putting

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.840
for audiences and critics.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.830
Regardless of how well Aquaman plays to its
strengths, it's still going to be the story

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:44.290
of a would-be king who talks to fish and does
battle with merpeople.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.769
It will probably never reach the universal
acclaim of something like The Dark Knight,

00:03:47.769 --> 00:03:51.100
a movie based on comic books and treated as
a hard-hitting police drama.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.020
Arthur Curry's adventures will simply never
have the same potential for crossover appeal.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.099
But here's the thing about a movie that leans
all the way into its own comic book silliness:

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:02.340
it's exactly what DC Films needs right now.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.650
While some discerning theatergoers might be
turned off by such a goofy outing as Aquaman,

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:11.380
it serves as the perfect antidote to the grim
self-seriousness of movies like Batman v Superman.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.580
"Tell me…

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.580
Do you bleed?"

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.840
We've watched Superman die and we've seen
Batman live long enough to become to villain.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:26.730
Even Wonder Woman's solo story didn't have
much time for levity once Diana arrived in

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:31.260
the trenches of World War I. Justice League
had a jarring tonal dissonance, trapped somewhere

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:32.440
between brooding and romping.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.900
"So your genius move is dying.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.920
You really are outta your mind."

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.240
"I'm not the one who brought a pitchfork."

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.360
But Aquaman is bright, wacky, and seems intent
on doing nothing beyond shooting fun straight

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.560
into its viewers' eyeballs.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.860
Arthur's tale is a feel-good story concerned
not with societal ethics or the meaning of

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.480
existence, but with his own journey to find
his own place and commit to what he cares

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:54.980
about.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:59.280
It will never make a shortlist of "Important
Films" or warrant major Oscar consideration,

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:00.550
but it isn't trying to.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:05.300
It's just fun, and in a year when Marvel slaughtered
half of all life in the universe, that makes

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.420
it a welcome dash of lightness and fun.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.340
"Show off.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.020
I coulda just peed on it."

